==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From an unattested {{bor|es|chb|-}} word variously described as the name of the surrounding region, the capital of the {{w|Muisca Confederation}}, the original name of the town of {{w|Funza}}, the name of a Muisca {{l|en|cacique}} or his title.

Various forms have been proposed as the original name, such as {{m|es|Bacatá}} (possibly a later invention <ref>Sylvia M. Broadbent, ''Situación del Bogotá chibcha'' in '''1974''', Revista Colombiana de Antropología</ref>); ''Bocatá'', meaning “fields’ end” and the name of a cacique <ref>'''Late 16th century''', Juan de Castellanos, ''Elegías de varones ilustres de Indias''</ref>; ''Bogote'', referring to the {{w|Bogotá Savannah}} and used as a hereditary title <ref>'''1626''', Pedro Simón, ''Noticias historiales de las conquistas de Tierra Firme en las Indias Occidentales''</ref>; {{m|es|Muequetá}}, supposedly from {{der|es|chb|muyquy||field}} + {{m|chb|ta||inside; field}}.

